}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"0ee0e581-3fed-4443-b0d4-dc7c7036800b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The operations of the algebra are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["CanonicalLieBracket"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/CanonicalLieBracket", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ce7bd210-4284-4ee8-a1a4-d139ae400c30"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["CanonicalLieCobracket"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/CanonicalLieCobracket", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "889ed8a1-2af0-4162-b7ca-2241f8f6d816"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["CyclicHochschildDifferential"]], 
    "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/CyclicHochschildDifferential", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "168ba3bf-762b-444b-aabd-981817e5ac69"],
 ", in the convention of ",
 StyleBox["pairing", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",
 CellFrameLabels->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {Inherited, 
    Cell[
     TextData[{
      "26.09.30: Design review - CanonicalLieBialgebra is an inert object \
around one Association, CanonicalLieBialgebra[<|\"Pairing\" -> pairing, \
\"EmptyWord\" -> b|>], and it has no recognizer (decision of R5e, \
2026-09-30). The constructor returns unevaluated unless it is given a \
GradedPairing object and a Boolean empty-word option, so that a constructor \
that built nothing does not look like an object, and the summary box attaches \
only to the built one. Since R7 (Pavel, 2026-10-01) the built object is \
recognized by its data, an Association with a \"Pairing\" holding a \
GradedPairing and an \"EmptyWord\" holding True or False, in every rule that \
takes it, and not by its head alone: CanonicalLieBialgebra[Normal[pairing]] \
matched CanonicalLieBialgebra[_Association] before, and Relations answered on \
it. The empty word is set once, on the algebra, and the Obstruction forms on \
it take no option. The algebra is the structure that Obstruction, Relations \
and RelationsQ take; those three are declared in HomotopyAlgebras with their \
A-infinity rules, and ChernSimons adds the rules of the string algebra, so \
the dependency between the parts runs one way. Together they replaced \
thirteen exports, every obstruction identical by value to the one it replaced \
on 95 cases. Prior art: the Wolfram Language has no dIBL or involutive bi-Lie \
structures; the verification suites test the relations on the circle in both \
conventions and with the empty word, on the two nilmanifold alphabets and on \
a derived alphabet.", "\n\n", 
       Cell[
        BoxData[
         GridBox[{{
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Edit"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationButton"]]], 
            StyleBox[
             RowBox[{
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "LastAnnotator"]], "pavel"}], 
             "TextAnnotator"], 
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Delete"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationRemoveButton"]]], ""}}, 
          GridBoxAlignment -> {
           "Columns" -> {Left, Left, Right, Right}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
          GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.68], 
              Scaled[0.15], 
              Scaled[0.02]}}]]], "\n"}], "TextAnnotation", 
     CellSize -> {590, Inherited}]}},
 CellTags->"TextAnnotation",
 CellID->671137923,ExpressionUUID->"72296aa2-993e-4851-b7b9-23d29da7d5ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The algebra is the structure that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Obstruction"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/Obstruction", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "acccdb37-e7cb-4c77-b3f9-51438d433d0f"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Relations"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/Relations", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "bf6491b5-27c9-4bd8-9bab-6f188d0d5f5f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["RelationsQ"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/RelationsQ", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b38df5a4-529a-469d-a090-ded050e48c5f"],
 " take."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ed475c0b-a3b7-4dc1-94b6-c1322cacea7c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its relations are ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Jacobi\>\""], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "939f2059-3b40-4ed1-a716-a87a26b25160"],
 " on three words, ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<CoJacobi\>\""], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "349b437b-a539-4db4-8e6e-11d9bd4480ff"],
 " on one, ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Drinfeld\>\""], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "202e14ea-6eab-49cc-a959-f1303cb943ed"],
 " on two and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Involutivity\>\""], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c4f50bae-aff6-46f3-9477-0c2eb870dc2b"],
 " on one, the defining identities of an involutive bi-Lie algebra. They \
involve the bracket and the co-bracket."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d9f4a5ad-8b1a-471c-8781-9ceb23e02dac"],

